          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Higgs bundle
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundle"} holomorphic vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            together with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} 1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
            of (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            of)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi \wedge \Phi = 0
          %p
            Higgs bundles play a central role in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Hodge+theory"} nonabelian Hodge theory
          %h2#Terminology Terminology
          %p
            The term was introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"} Nigel Hitchin
            as a reference to roughly analogous structures in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            related to the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+field"} Higgs field
          %blockquote
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Witten08"}> Witten 08, remark 2.1
              ): As an aside, one may ask how closely related
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} particle physics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+fields"} Higgs fields
              in particle physics are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+fields"} scalar fields
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-form"} one-form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (valued in each case in some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
              of the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D4+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N = 4 supersymmetric gauge theory
              via a sort of twisting procedure (similar to the procedure that leads from N = 2 supersymmetric gauge theory to Donaldson theory). In this twisting procedure, some of the Higgs-like scalar fields of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 4
              super Yang-Mills theory are indeed converted into the Higgs field that enters in Hitchin’s equations.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "#KapustinWitten06"} Kapustin-Witten 06
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              This gives a reasonable justification for the terminology.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_components In components
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundle"} holomorphic vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_M
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_M
          %p
            A
            %strong Higgs field
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is an
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_M
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi M
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Phi : \mathcal{E}\to \Omega^1_M\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_M}\mathcal{E}
          %p
            satisfying the integrability condition
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi\wedge\Phi = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\Phi)
            is then called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Higgs bundle
          %p
            (Notice that this is similar to but crucially different the definition of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
            on a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is just
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo +
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}\phi + \Phi\wedge\Phi = 0
          %p
            Higgs bundles can be considered as a limiting case of a (holomorphic)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            in the limit in which its exterior differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\Phi
            is small in comparison to the exterior square
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi\wedge\Phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi dz
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d u/dz = A(z)u
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(z)
            is a matrix of connection can be rescaled by putting a small parameter in front of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi dz
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d u/dz
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(z)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi\wedge\Phi = 0
          %p
            In fact, there is a notion interpolating between flat connections and Higgs bundles due Deligne, the Deligne’s
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lambda-connection"} connection
          %h3#formulation_in_dgeometry Formulation in D-geometry
          %p
            Analogous to how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+stack"} de Rham stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi inf
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{inf} X = X_{dR}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"}> homotopy
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by the first order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi Dol
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{Dol}
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
            of the 0-section of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (
            %a{:href => "#Simpson96"}> Simpson 96
            ).
          %p
            Now a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+vector+bundle"} flat vector bundle
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is essentially just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+stack"} de Rham stack
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+bundle"} Higgs bundle
            is essentially just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi Dol
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{Dol}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+group"} algebraic group
            over
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi Dol
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi ss
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}(X_{dR}, \mathbf{B}G)
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbf{H}(X_{Dol}, \mathbf{B}G)^{ss,0}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the superscript on the right denotes restriction to semistable Higgs bundles with vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Raboso14"} Raboso 14, theorem 4.2
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#stability Stability
          %p
            For a Higgs bundle to admit a harmonic metric (…) it needs to be
            %em stable
            (…).
          %p
            Stability is defined similarly to stability for holomorphic vector bundles except that instead of quantifying over all proper non-zero sub-bundles, one only considers proper
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            invariant sub-bundles. So in particular for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi=0
          %h3#in_nonabelian_hodge_theory In nonabelian Hodge theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Hodge+theory"} nonabelian Hodge theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of stable Higgs bundles over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is identified with that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+linear+group"} special linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(n,\mathbb{C})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#rank_1 Rank 1
          %p
            In the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            1, hence is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is simply any holomorphic 1-form. This case is also called that of an
            = succeed "." do
              %strong abelian Higgs bundle
          %h3#bundles_of_holomorphic_forms Bundles of holomorphic forms
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^{k,0}(X)
            for odd
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{\bullet,0}(X)
            becomes a Higgs bundle when equipped with the endomorphis-valued 1-form which sends a holomorphic vector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            to the wedge product operation with the contraction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
          %p
            This is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Seaman98"}> Seaman 98
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+system"} Hitchin system
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Hodge+theory"} nonabelian Hodge theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+recursion"} topological recursion
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of Higgs bundles over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
            is one of the principal topics in works of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"} Nigel Hitchin
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"} Carlos Simpson
            in late 1980-s and 1990-s (and later Ron Donagi, Tony Pantev, etc….), hence also known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Hitchin moduli space
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"}> N.J. Hitchin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable bundles and integrable systems
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=89a:32021"} MR89a:32021
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1215/S0012-7094-87-05408-1"} doi
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.dmj/1077305506"} euclid
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The self-duality equations on a Riemann surface
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=887284"} MR887284
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1112/plms/s3-55.1.59"} doi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 131
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104200841"} euclid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higgs bundles and local systems
                %strong 75
                (1992), p. 5-95,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=PMIHES_1992__75__5_0"} numdam
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=94d:32027"} MR94d:32027
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ludmil+Katzarkov"}> Ludmil Katzarkov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"} Dmitri Orlov
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"} Tony Pantev
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Higgs bundles and D-branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cimat.mx/Eventos/moduli_spaces2013"} link
                %a{:href => "http://www.cimat.mx/Eventos/moduli_spaces2013/img/tony_pantev.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                S. B. Bradlow, O. García-Prada, P. B. Gothen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em WHAT IS…a Higgs Bundle?
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/200708/tx070800980p.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Murray"}> Michael Murray
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higgs fields, bundle gerbes and string structures
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Baraglia"}> David Baraglia
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic Higgs bundles and the affine Toda equations
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.6421"} arxiv:1011.6421
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                , around lemma 6.4.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on supersymmetric and holomorphic field theories in dimension 2 and 4
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/dennisfest/"} Geometric and Algebraic Structures in Mathematics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.4234"} arXiv:1111.4234
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Swoboda"}> Jan Swoboda
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Moduli Spaces of Higgs Bundles – Old and New
              %strong 123
              (2021) 65–130 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1365/s13291-021-00229-1"}> doi:10.1365/s13291-021-00229-1
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Donu Arapura,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/101326/what-is-the-current-state-of-the-mathematics-of-higgs-fields/101347#101347"} MO comment on Higgs bundles
            %li
              %p
                math.stackexchange:
                %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/2498255/difference-between-higgs-bundle-and-vector-bundle-with-connection"} difference-between-higgs-bundle-and-vector-bundle-with-connection
          %p Discussion of the topology of the moduli space of Higgs bundles is in
          %ul
            %li#Rayan18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Rayan"}> Steven Rayan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Aspects of the topology and combinatorics of Higgs bundle moduli spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.05732"} arXiv:1809.05732
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi Dol
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{Dol}
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Simpson96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Hodge filtration on nonabelian cohomology
              %p
                1492538 (99g:14028) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9604005"}> arXiv:9604005
                )
            %li#Raboso14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Garc%C3%ADa+Raboso"}> Alberto García Raboso
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A twisted nonabelian Hodge correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.toronto.edu/agraboso/files/TwistedNAHT_Talk_Handout.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p Discussion of the example of homolorphic forms is in
          %ul
            %li#Seaman98
              Walter Seaman,
              %em Higgs Bundles and Holomorphic Forms
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9811097"}> arXiv:9811097
              )
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+duality"} geometric Langlands duality
            includes
          %ul
            %li#KapustinWitten06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Electric-Magnetic Duality And The Geometric Langlands Program
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0604151"} arXiv:hep-th/0604151
            %li#Witten08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em Mirror Symmetry, Hitchin’s Equations, And Langlands Duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.0999"}> arXiv:0802.0999
                )
          %p
            The following paper starts with a survey of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Hodge+correspondence"} nonabelian Hodge correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              Peter B. Gothen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higgs bundles and the real symplectic group
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.4175"} arXiv:1102.4175
          %h3#relation_to_manifolds
            Relation to
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(7)
          %p
            Relating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+Spin%287%29-manifolds"} M-theory on Spin(7)-manifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+Spin%287%29-manifolds"} F-theory on Spin(7)-manifolds
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+bundles"} Higgs bundles
          %ul
            %li#CHRTZ20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"} Jonathan Heckman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gianluca+Zoccarato"} Gianluca Zoccarato
              %em Geometric Unification of Higgs Bundle Vacua
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.13682"}> arXiv:2003.13682
              )
          %h3#mirror_symmetry Mirror symmetry
          %ul
            %li
              Victoria Hoskins, Simon Pepin Lehalleur.
              %em Motivic mirror symmetry for Higgs bundles
              (2022). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.15393"}> arXiv:2205.15393
              ).
        .revisedby
